{:adr-id "2607154500"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-960 — Personal-Care Salon/Service Operations Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 960 (Other personal service activities) -- laundry/dry-
  cleaning, hairdressing/beauty salons, funeral/burial services, and
  other personal-care services not elsewhere classified. Second and
  final Wave 4 actor in the ISIC-95/96 personal-services cluster (after
  isic-952 repair-shop coordination). Fresh scaffold under the
  verified-redo discipline (ADR-2607152500), mirrored on isic-952's
  module shape."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor for personal-care salon/service back-office
   administration. Closed five-op allowlist, all :effect :propose:
   schedule-service-appointment, coordinate-service-status-update,
   coordinate-supply-request, schedule-staff-shift-proposal,
   flag-safety-concern (always escalates, no client-verification
   required since it is facility-level). An op outside this set is the
   SAME failure mode as forbidden-scope content, not a separate
   carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Three HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks: (1) client/appointment-
   record unverified -- target must be independently :registered?/
   :verified? in the store, never trusted from the proposal's own
   claim (exempt for :flag-safety-concern); (2) effect-not-propose --
   any :effect other than :propose is a claim to directly actuate
   outside governance; (3) scope-exclusion -- any proposal (any op)
   touching service-technique/treatment decisions, health/sanitation-
   compliance determinations, client health/allergy-risk clinical
   judgments, or safety-authority territory, evaluated unconditionally
   via a lower-cased EN+JA substring/regex scan combined into a single
   explicit boolean (in-forbidden-territory) that is what the check
   actually returns -- verified free of the isic-920 batch's dead-code
   bug class where an English-language check was computed but its
   result discarded. flag-safety-concern is exempt from the content
   scan since it always escalates rather than auto-committing."
  :module-shape
  "personalcareops.store (MemStore, string-keyed client/service
   directory, append-only ledger), advisor (mock + real-LLM seam),
   governor (three HARD checks), phase (0->3 rollout), operation
   (langgraph-clj StateGraph: intake->advise->govern->decide->
   commit|hold|escalate), sim (demo driver, 5 scenarios)."}
 :consequences
 ["Registry entry corrected in place (exact-text edit of the existing"
  " {:id \"960\" ...} block, independently EDN-parse-validated before"
  " and after the edit via a fresh Contents API fetch): :repo/"
  ":business-id updated to cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-960,"
  " :maturity :implemented, :robotics stripped from"
  " :required-technologies"
  "Actor repo cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-960 scaffolded and"
  " pushed to main, public, full governance file set present"
  "Test suite (store/governor/operation/phase) and sim demo"
  " independently re-verified against the live repo by this landing"
  " session, not just the building session's self-report"
  "Governor scope-exclusion check confirmed free of the isic-920"
  " dead-code bug class"
  "This ADR pair landed in a follow-up step after the building"
  " session's claimed ADR path (2607161900, an out-of-sequence"
  " tomorrow-dated number) was never actually pushed anywhere;"
  " content reconstructed from the live actor repo source"]
